# Language-bar hygiene (GitHub Linguist)
#
# DeusRidet's product body is the C++/CUDA inference engine under src/.
# The Python under tools/ is an evaluation / replay / benchmark scaffold
# (live scoring harnesses, audio-analysis probes, fixture builders). It is
# our own code, but it is not the product — it exists to measure and
# reproduce the C++/CUDA core. Excluding it from the language statistics
# makes the GitHub language bar reflect the project body, not the harness.
#
# We use `linguist-detectable=false` (not `linguist-vendored`) because the
# scripts are authored by us, not third-party: they should simply not be
# counted toward the language breakdown, without being mislabelled as
# vendored or generated.
tools/**/*.py linguist-detectable=false

# Generated / vendored build artifacts that may sit in the tree should also
# never drive the language bar.
third_party/** linguist-vendored
